  "title": "Answer: no theory of intelligence, though thoughts can cause thoughts",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "f51dd7b7-28c7-4be3-98f7-04c81559c86d",
      "text": "The view has no theory of intelligence. It holds that reasoning is in part mental causation: a thought that something answers a mathematical problem is caused in part by other mathematical thoughts, not only by brain events.",
